Open the next transaction only after acknowledging the previous Submitted

The export keeps an accepted candidate, and refuses a new transaction open
with EBUSY, until its Submitted event is acknowledged; it serves a
connection's requests in order. A record unit now starts only once intake
has handled the previous Submitted and an ack through its sequence is
queued, so the ack always precedes the next walk and open. Before, an
outstanding earlier ack, an early-settled Submitted not yet reached by
intake, or an ack held behind an unfetched announcement let the next open
go first. Scripted regressions log the ack before the next walk in both
the shared-drain and held-ack cases, and fail without the gate.
